  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "32463338",
      "title": "Services & Standalone Components",
      "lectureOrder": 670,
      "videoOrder": 616,
      "sourceHash": "15d4effd897e7c7a77e8d37b1be14308e4dfa057b1784d8ddbce540c798c7e38",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.89,
          "en": "Speaker: Now I wanna take a brief look at services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.89,
          "end": 6.69,
          "en": "with standalone components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.69,
          "end": 9.54,
          "en": "I do have one service in this demo app and it is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.54,
          "end": 12.24,
          "en": "a service, as you would always define it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.24,
          "end": 15.3,
          "en": "It's a class decorated with at injectable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.3,
          "end": 18.42,
          "en": "where I provide an object with the providedIn property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.42,
          "end": 19.95,
          "en": "set to root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.95,
          "end": 23.238,
          "en": "This yet makes sure that this service is provided to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.238,
          "end": 26.22,
          "en": "all components of your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.22,
          "end": 29.13,
          "en": "All your components and directives can inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.13,
          "end": 32.79,
          "en": "this service and all those components and directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.79,
          "end": 36.453,
          "en": "will operate on the same object based on that service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.405,
          "end": 40.95,
          "en": "Now this works just fine with standalone components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.95,
          "end": 42.24,
          "en": "as you can clearly tell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.24,
          "end": 45.03,
          "en": "because no adjustments were needed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.03,
          "end": 48.03,
          "en": "However you might recall that this is not the only way of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.03,
          "end": 49.98,
          "en": "providing services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.98,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "Instead of doing it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 53.85,
          "en": "which is the recommended way, typically though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.85,
          "end": 56.58,
          "en": "You could have also added this service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.58,
          "end": 59.58,
          "en": "to the provider's array of a module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.58,
          "end": 61.26,
          "en": "and that would've been fine as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.26,
          "end": 64.17,
          "en": "And it would've also made that service available to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.17,
          "end": 67.98,
          "en": "all components and directives and it would've made available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.98,
          "end": 70.68,
          "en": "a single object of that service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.68,
          "end": 73.41,
          "en": "What you can also do, and what you could do before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.41,
          "end": 75.99,
          "en": "standalone components as well is you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.99,
          "end": 79.5,
          "en": "go to a component and add the provider's property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.5,
          "end": 82.32,
          "en": "to this components decorator object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.32,
          "end": 84.12,
          "en": "And again, this is not new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.12,
          "end": 87.18,
          "en": "You could do this with Angular two already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.18,
          "end": 89.97,
          "en": "And then you can also add your analytics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 89.97,
          "end": 94.11,
          "en": "service here, add import to the file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.11,
          "end": 96.03,
          "en": "and then point at the class here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 96.03,
          "end": 98.25,
          "en": "And if you save this, you will notice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.25,
          "end": 100.923,
          "en": "that this still works as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.88,
          "end": 104.88,
          "en": "So that's another way of providing services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.88,
          "end": 107.28,
          "en": "Now the difference is that if you add a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.28,
          "end": 109.035,
          "en": "service to a component like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.035,
          "end": 112.53,
          "en": "every component gets its own object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 112.53,
          "end": 116.1,
          "en": "So if you use the same service for multiple instances",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.1,
          "end": 118.86,
          "en": "of a component, you get multiple instances of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.86,
          "end": 119.75999999999999,
          "en": "service as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 119.75999999999999,
          "end": 122.58,
          "en": "And there is no shared state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 122.58,
          "end": 125.25,
          "en": "Sometimes that's needed, often that's not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 125.25,
          "end": 127.2,
          "en": "Therefore you rarely do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 127.2,
          "end": 130.62,
          "en": "This behavior is not new though, it always worked like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.62,
          "end": 133.02,
          "en": "I just wanted to mention again that you can still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 133.02,
          "end": 136.413,
          "en": "use it even if you are using standalone components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 137.55,
          "end": 140.97,
          "en": "Now, if still, for whatever reason, you don't wanna provide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.97,
          "end": 144.39,
          "en": "a service globally by adding providedIn here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 144.39,
          "end": 148.11,
          "en": "you can also bring back the old feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.11,
          "end": 151.47,
          "en": "of adding it to a provider's array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.47,
          "end": 154.07999999999998,
          "en": "Previously you added the ng module with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 154.07999999999998,
          "end": 157.35,
          "en": "a provider's object which was an array of services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 157.35,
          "end": 160.86,
          "en": "Now, in such a application that doesn't have modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 160.86,
          "end": 163.59,
          "en": "you can go to the bootstrap application function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 163.59,
          "end": 167.01,
          "en": "and add a second object, which allows you to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 167.01,
          "end": 169.17000000000002,
          "en": "provide some configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 169.17000000000002,
          "end": 172.26,
          "en": "At the moment there's only one property you can set though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 172.26,
          "end": 174.9,
          "en": "and that's the provider's property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 174.9,
          "end": 177.84,
          "en": "And here you can do exactly what you would imagine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 177.84,
          "end": 181.74,
          "en": "You can add your globally provided services here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 181.74,
          "end": 185.55,
          "en": "So here I can also add my analytics service like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.55,
          "end": 188.566,
          "en": "Add a import to the file, add the class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.566,
          "end": 190.92,
          "en": "make sure you don't have providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 190.92,
          "end": 192.81,
          "en": "in the details component anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 192.81,
          "end": 196.2,
          "en": "And still with this kind of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 196.2,
          "end": 200.613,
          "en": "you will see that if I open this, my service still works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 201.87,
          "end": 203.67000000000002,
          "en": "So this is the equivalent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.67000000000002,
          "end": 207.12,
          "en": "of having a provider's array in ng module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 207.12,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "If you wanna provide some service globally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 212.49,
          "en": "you can add it here with this second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 212.49,
          "end": 215.46,
          "en": "that's passed to bootstrap application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 215.46,
          "end": 218.73,
          "en": "Now here, this is really not needed, therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 218.73,
          "end": 220.29,
          "en": "I'll comment this out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 220.29,
          "end": 221.79,
          "en": "Actually, you could do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 221.79,
          "end": 224.7,
          "en": "but it's not needed because here the best way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 224.7,
          "end": 229.5,
          "en": "of providing this service is to add this providedIn syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 229.5,
          "end": 231.45,
          "en": "Still, I wanted to mention it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 231.45,
          "end": 234.03,
          "en": "because it is important to understand how you can work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.03,
          "end": 236.883,
          "en": "with services and standalone components.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
